**Set it up on your Xiaomi, Redmi or POCO:**

1. **Install CrookCatcher** from <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.harteg.crookcatcher&referrer=utm_source%3Dwebsite%26utm_medium%3Dguide%26utm_campaign%3Dxiaomi-who-tried-to-unlock" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Play</a>. There's no account to create.
2. **Allow Device admin.** CrookCatcher uses this permission only to know when an unlock attempt fails.
3. **Allow camera and location access.**
4. **Connect a Gmail account** for the alert emails. CrookCatcher can only *send* emails from it, not read them.
5. **Test it.** Lock your phone, enter a wrong PIN on purpose, then unlock it. Your own photo should appear in the app and your inbox.

### Two extra settings on Xiaomi phones

HyperOS is strict about apps that run in the background. Without these two settings it may stop CrookCatcher after a while, and you'd get no photo when it matters.

1. **Allow autostart.** Go to `Settings > Apps > Permissions > Background autostart` and turn it on for CrookCatcher.
2. **Remove battery restrictions.** During setup, CrookCatcher asks you to tap **Manage battery settings**. Choose **No restrictions** on the screen that opens.

Menu names can differ slightly between HyperOS versions. If you can't find Background autostart, search for "autostart" in Settings. Then repeat the wrong-PIN test a day later to check that it still works.

Since 2014, CrookCatcher has been downloaded more than 12 million times, and it takes around 1.2 million intruder photos a day.

