## Frequently Asked Questions

### Q: Does Xiaomi have a built-in intruder selfie feature?
A: No. Xiaomi's documentation describes no feature that photographs someone who enters a wrong lock screen or App lock password. To get a photo, you need an app like CrookCatcher.

### Q: How many wrong PIN attempts does a Xiaomi phone allow?
A: Xiaomi doesn't publish the numbers. After several wrong guesses the lock screen shows a countdown, and the person has to wait for it to end before trying again.

### Q: Can I see failed unlock attempts on a Redmi or POCO phone?
A: No. Redmi and POCO phones run the same HyperOS as Xiaomi phones. They count wrong guesses only to time the lockouts, and never show them to you.

### Q: Why did CrookCatcher stop taking photos on my Xiaomi?
A: Most often HyperOS has stopped it in the background. Turn on **Background autostart** for CrookCatcher and set its battery setting to **No restrictions**, as described above. Also note that after a restart, the phone has to be unlocked once before any app can use the camera.

### Q: Can a thief turn off my Xiaomi from the lock screen?
A: On most Xiaomi phones, yes. Xiaomi's help page for the Redmi Note 13 says a password to shut down isn't a standard feature. That's why it helps to get a photo and location the moment someone enters a wrong PIN, before the phone is switched off. See [how to stop power off and airplane mode from the lock screen](/blog/block-power-menu) for what you can do.

### Q: Will the person see that they were photographed?
A: CrookCatcher works in the background without a camera preview. Recent Android versions show a small indicator while the camera is in use; that's a system feature apps can't hide.

